WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.000
Hi this is Presh Talwalkar.

00:00:02.300 --> 00:00:04.000
Warren Buffett
once challenged Bill Gates

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:06.500
to a special dice game like the following:

00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:10.300
the dices each had six faces that were equally likely to show up

00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:13.260
but the numbers were different than a standard dice.

00:00:13.260 --> 00:00:17.700
One of the dices had all 3s on all of its six faces.

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:22.760
Another one had 0 on two of
its faces and 4 on four of its faces.

00:00:22.760 --> 00:00:27.060
A third dice had an equal number of 1s and 5s,

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:33.100
and a fourth dice had 2 on four of its faces and 6 on two of its faces.

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:35.160
So here's how the game works:

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:37.880
you and I are each going to pick a different one of these dices.

00:00:37.880 --> 00:00:40.600
We're not going to pick the same dices; we're going to pick different dices.

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:42.920
We're then going to roll against each other,

00:00:42.920 --> 00:00:45.780
and the person who gets the higher number gets the point.

00:00:46.220 --> 00:00:53.820
You then repeat that many many times so that the person who rolls the highest number of points over many rolls is going to win the game.

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:58.420
I'm going to graciously offer you to let you pick your dice first.

00:00:58.420 --> 00:01:01.100
Which one do you want?

00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:05.100
Give this problem a try and when you ready keep watching the video for the solution

00:01:08.580 --> 00:01:14.760
So let's analyze this game, suppose you pick the dice with all threes.

00:01:14.760 --> 00:01:23.880
What I am going to do is I am going to pick the dice which has zero on two of its spaces, and four on four of its spaces.

00:01:23.880 --> 00:01:26.660
What's going to happen if we roll against each other?

00:01:26.660 --> 00:01:33.400
Well, if I roll a zero which happens two of the sixth times, I'm going to lose to you because you are always going to roll a three.

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:38.660
However, in the four out of the six times I roll a four I'm actually going to beat you.

00:01:38.660 --> 00:01:47.740
So I'm going to beat you, two-thirds of the time, so if you pick a dice which has all threes, you're going to lose to me two-thirds of the time.

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:56.280
So now suppose you know this strategy and you say, "Well, why don't I pick the dice that has two zeros and four fours?"

00:01:56.280 --> 00:02:04.720
Well if you are going to pick that dice, then I am going to pick the dice that has three ones and three fives.

00:02:04.720 --> 00:02:08.180
It's a little harder to analyze what happens when we roll these two dice

00:02:08.180 --> 00:02:10.180
against each other but it's not too complicated.

00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:18.300
Now, I'm going to win if I roll a five because anytime I roll a five it's higher than you rolling a zero or a four.

00:02:18.340 --> 00:02:22.900
So in three out of the six cases I'm going to roll five and I'm guaranteed to win.

00:02:22.900 --> 00:02:26.100
Now when I roll the one, in three out of six cases,

00:02:26.140 --> 00:02:31.580
I'm only going to beat you in the two out of the six cases that you roll a zero as well.

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:33.580
So in summary,

00:02:33.880 --> 00:02:37.360
I'm going to win 3/6 times 1 when I roll a 5,

00:02:37.580 --> 00:02:42.680
plus 3/6, when I roll a zero--when I roll a ONE, times 2/6 when you roll a zero.

00:02:43.660 --> 00:02:45.580
So this nets out to 2/3

00:02:45.580 --> 00:02:47.580
of the time, I'm going to win. So

00:02:47.580 --> 00:02:49.580
once again,  your die that you pick

00:02:49.580 --> 00:02:51.580
is going to lose  to my die 2/3 of the time.

00:02:51.580 --> 00:02:53.580
 

00:02:53.580 --> 00:02:55.580
This argument continues. Let's suppose you pick

00:02:55.580 --> 00:02:56.840
the die that I just had,

00:02:57.300 --> 00:02:59.920
Well in that case I'm going to pick the next die which has

00:03:00.220 --> 00:03:03.300
2 on four of its faces and 6 on two of its faces.

00:03:03.580 --> 00:03:05.380
We can do a similar calculation.

00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:08.820
I'm going to win two out of the six times when I roll a 6,

00:03:08.820 --> 00:03:09.620
guaranteed.

00:03:10.140 --> 00:03:12.140
And I'm also going to win if I roll a 2,

00:03:12.140 --> 00:03:14.140
which is 4/6 of the time,

00:03:14.140 --> 00:03:17.220
against your 1, which happens 3/6 of the time.

00:03:17.940 --> 00:03:21.640
So once again, I'm going to beat your die 2/3 of the time.

00:03:21.640 --> 00:03:23.640
 

00:03:30.180 --> 00:03:32.580
Now I'm going to win whenever I roll--

00:03:32.860 --> 00:03:36.860
--whenever YOU roll a 2, which happens 4/6 of the time,

00:03:36.860 --> 00:03:40.460
so once again your die is losing to my die 2/3 of the time.

00:03:41.260 --> 00:03:42.440
So what we've shown

00:03:42.700 --> 00:03:44.220
is that each die

00:03:44.220 --> 00:03:47.460
is actually going to lose 2/3 of the tme to another die.

00:03:47.940 --> 00:03:50.640
And this is what's known as non-transitive dice.

00:03:51.320 --> 00:03:53.520
Each die can be beaten like another

00:03:53.600 --> 00:03:55.440
like a game of rock, paper, scissors.

00:03:55.860 --> 00:03:59.000
This is a cyclical game, and that's why it's non-transitive.

00:04:00.720 --> 00:04:03.660
The first person who selects the die is always going to be at a

00:04:03.660 --> 00:04:05.480
disadvantage to someone who picks

00:04:05.480 --> 00:04:06.560
this second

00:04:06.820 --> 00:04:08.820
because each can be beaten by another.

00:04:10.560 --> 00:04:13.560
As the story goes, Warren Buffet challenged Bill Gates to this and said,

00:04:13.560 --> 00:04:15.560
"Go ahead. Why don't you select first?"

00:04:16.280 --> 00:04:19.240
Bill Gates was smart enough to say, "Let me inspect the dice."

00:04:19.540 --> 00:04:22.500
And he figured out that there was something weird going on with the dice.

00:04:22.500 --> 00:04:24.500
 

00:04:25.780 --> 00:04:27.780
Thanks for watching.

